# Swampcycling searches for a "Swamp card" - by land type (CR 205.3i, 702.29e): Bayou is a Swamp Forest, so it can be found (the
# existing scenario finds a basic Swamp), while an Island and a Forest cannot (the refusals). Then a second Troll is swampcycled on
# turn 3 and the search is answered with nothing (a quality search may find nothing, CR 701.23b): it is still discarded for {1}.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Troll of Khazad-dûm
Troll of Khazad-dûm
Island x4
Bayou
Forest
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Troll of Khazad-dûm.Activate
! Bot1.Search(Island)
! Bot1.Search(Forest)
Bot1.Search(Bayou)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Bayou.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Troll of Khazad-dûm.Activate
Bot1.Search()

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Troll of Khazad-dûm; Troll of Khazad-dûm
Bot1.Battlefield = Island; Bayou
